@node "WalkThrough" "Walk Through Guide to FileKiller"
@{b}@{fg shine}________________________________________________________________________@{ub}@{fg text}

@{b}Walk through guide@{ub}
@{b}________________________________________________________________________@{ub}

As soon as @{b}FileKiller@{ub} is started it will request a file. You can enter either
a name or number for a file here;  a list of the currently tagged files is
also displayed to help you remember the file. After you have entered a file,
it will be checked if it is validated, and if not you will be asked if you
want to validate it.

(Note: a file number isn't displayed on the tagged file list due to a bug in
Zeus.. You'll need to copy the full name if you want to use the tagged list)

You'll then be requested if you want to search for the uploader to send them
either a warning message or a "thank you!" message. This option should really
have also had the option to alter the users current down/upload credits, but
I can't find a way to do it short of rewritting this program in assembler...
Use the configuration option @{"USERMSGAREA" link "Config-USERMSGAREA" 0} to specify where the message to the
user is posted. In the default configuration it's set as area one.

Then you are asked if you want to make the file a free download.

Next, you can write a comment onto the end of the file comment (which will
also be displayed on a "Thank You!" message to the user)

BTW: it's here, at the end of the program that the messages are created and
posted (using the Zeus:Bin/PostMsg program.  I may add built in message
posting, but I don't see much point really :)


 @{i}Sorry about this quick'n'cheap walk through guide, but as I'm
 going to be re-writting the user interface I don't think there is much
 point doing a full document (like there will be for the next release
 version)  =)@{ui}
@endnode

@node "Config" "Configuration"
@{b}@{fg shine}________________________________________________________________________@{ub}@{fg text}

@{b}Configuration@{ub}                       @{b}Doors:FileKiller/FileKiller.CFG@{ub}
@{b}________________________________________________________________________@{ub}

All configuration options are specified in the file
Doors:FileKiller/FileKiller.CFG


    @{b}@{i}@{u}Section              Keyword in config file@{ub}@{ui}@{uu}

    @{"Comments File      " link "Config-CommentsFile" 0}  COMMENTS
    @{"File Announce Area " link "Config-AnnouceArea" 0}  ANNOUNCEAREA
    @{"File Announce Text " link "Config-AnnounceText" 0}  ANNOUNCETEXT
    @{"User's Message Area" link "Config-USERMSGAREA" 0}  USERMSGAREA
@endnode

@node "Config-CommentsFile" "Comments File  "
@{b}@{fg shine}________________________________________________________________________@{ub}@{fg text}

@{b}Comments File                 Default: Doors:FileKiller/Comments.txt@{ub}
@{b}________________________________________________________________________@{ub}

@{b}@{fg shine}Keyword:@{ub}@{fg text} COMMENTS

This option points to a file (Default: Doors:FileKiller/Comments.txt) which
contains a list of comments available when you opt to add a comment to a
file.

Example of using the Keyword;

 @{fg shine}------- 8< --------@{fg text}
 COMMENTS Doors:FileKiller/Comments.txt
 @{fg shine}------- 8< --------@{fg text}

The structure of the file @{b}must@{ub} be followed carefully, as there is very little
checking involved when reading it!

(Everything must be right at the left side, i.e. a left margin of 0
characters.  The reason there is a 1 character space here is because of
Heddley's reformatting)

@{fg shine} <Number of comments>
 <Comment1>
 <Comment2>
 <Comment3>
 <Comment4>
 <Commentx>@{fg text}

for example:


 @{fg shine}------- 8< --------@{fg text}
 3
 Amazing file!
 I've been looking for this for ages!
 Download this file if you haven't got it =)
 @{fg shine}------- 8< --------@{fg text}


Please bear in mind a limit of 40 characters across.  Most FileListers are
set to display 44 characters in one line of a file description so that is the
limit I've set FileKiller to use, after it has added two characters ("* " and
" *") to the comment to make the comment stand out against the file
description. If your text goes over the limit, both the left and right
characters out of the range will be lost, as the comments are centred, @{i}then@{ui}
cut to 44 characters from the middle out..
@endnode

@node "Config-AnnouceArea" "Configuration - Announce Area"
@{b}@{fg shine}________________________________________________________________________@{ub}@{fg text}

@{b}File Announce Area@{ub}
@{b}________________________________________________________________________@{ub}

@{b}@{fg shine}Keyword:@{ub}@{fg text} ANNOUNCEAREA

With this keyword, you can specify which area the message created when you
choose `Announce File' will go in.

Example:

@{fg shine} ------------ 8< -cut-here----@{fg text}

 ANNOUNCEAREA 3     ; my local points/BBS callers only area

@{fg shine} ------------ 8< -cut-here----@{fg text}
@endnode

@node "Config-UserMsgArea" "User's Message Area"
@{b}@{fg shine}________________________________________________________________________@{ub}@{fg text}

@{b}User's Message Area@{ub}
@{b}________________________________________________________________________@{ub}

@{b}@{fg shine}Keyword:@{ub}@{fg text} USERMSGAREA

With this keyword, you can specify which area the message created when you
choose to send a user a Warn or "Thank You!" will go in.

Example:

@{fg shine} ------------ 8< -cut-here----@{fg text}

 USERMSGAREA 3     ; Area with PRIVATE messages enabled!

@{fg shine} ------------ 8< -cut-here----@{fg text}
@endnode

